	{
		"DESCRIPTION": "Flat-top HEX ground tileset at 32 px: 75 unique hexes from a 20x10 lattice over region temp2's ground. Buildings are absent by construction -- the cut is taken from WorldMapProps' patched ground, which paints the nine structures out (7 houses, 2 towers), verified as 482 building-only pixels in the source art against 0 here. GEOMETRY: a flat-top hex pre-stretched for pitch 60 has a square world footprint, so each frame is 32x32 with vertices on whole pixels at (32,16) (24,32) (8,32) (0,16) (8,0) (24,0) and every slanted edge a 1:2 slope. A hex is 2 world units wide under the 16 px world unit, so map columns advance 1.5 units, rows 2, odd columns dropped 1. The SHEET stays a rectangular grid of 32 px frames, which is why the importer, hashes and id ledger read it unchanged. PROVENANCE: the source carries only 16 px of information per tile, so it was upscaled 2x NEAREST before cutting -- every source pixel is a 2x2 block and nothing is invented. That gives the silhouette genuine 32 px resolution over honestly-blocky content. Hex-native art will supersede this; it exists to settle framing and lattice geometry.",
